<article{{ attributes }}>

  {# ── Hero ── #}
  <div class="tamu-collection-hero" style="background-image: url('https://digitalcollections.library.tamu.edu/iiif/2/34d%2Fimage-utf-8-cmlrsc00181-eacdb2b9-d3a7-4ece-85b8-4e01c1a27170.jp2/20,18,7004,4586/full/0/default.jpg'); background-size: cover; background-position: center;">
    <div class="tamu-collection-hero__overlay">
      <div class="container">
        <h1 class="tamu-collection-hero__title">About Our Digital Collections</h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {# ── Body ── #}
  <div class="container tamu-about-body">
    {{ title_suffix }}

    <div class="tamu-about-body__intro">
      <h2>Our collections are comprised of a range of media covering many topics</h2>
      <p>Digital Collections contains thousands of items from Texas A&amp;M University Libraries.
      While only a fraction of materials from the Libraries' holdings are represented, the site
      reflects the distinction and diversity of the collections held by Cushing Memorial Library.</p>
    </div>

    <hr class="tamu-about-body__divider">

    <section class="tamu-about-body__section">
      <h2>Using our collections</h2>

      <h3>Rights Statements and Creative Commons Licenses</h3>
      <p>Texas A&amp;M University Libraries uses <a href="https://rightsstatements.org">rightsstatements.org</a>
      and Creative Commons licenses to help users understand the rights status of works in our collections.
      Each work includes a Rights Statement field with a badge representing its rights status; clicking the
      badge reveals more details. Some works also include a Rights Details field with additional information
      about the rights held in and over the resource. For questions about the rights status of an item,
      contact Cushing Memorial Library.</p>

      <h3>International Image Interoperability Framework (IIIF)</h3>
      <p>All content — metadata and images — is available as IIIF manifests, backed by a IIIF Image Server.
      This lets researchers explore detailed, zoomable images directly on this site, and also use the content
      in outside tools such as Canopy and Mirador, embed it on third-party websites, or query the data
      programmatically.</p>
      <p>The link to a collection's or work's manifest is available on every page under
      <strong>View IIIF Manifest</strong>.</p>
      <p>Learn more about IIIF and related projects on the
      <a href="https://iiif.io">IIIF website</a>.</p>
    </section>

  </div>

</article>
